&lt;p&gt;As a Staff Software Engineer, you&#39;ll help lead two important areas for GitLab Security: the data layer behind our vulnerability and dependency management capabilities, and our move toward services outside the GitLab monolith. You&#39;ll design and develop systems that ingest, store, index, and query security report data, including integrations with key third-party systems. With a strong focus on PostgreSQL and scalable backend design, your work will support security features delivered by teams across GitLab.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You&#39;ll take ownership of large deliverables from early ideas through implementation, working directly with product, design, frontend, and engineering partners to shape the technical and product roadmap. You&#39;ll stay hands-on across GitLab&#39;s Ruby on Rails application and newer services, including greenfield projects, while helping the team build its expertise in modular service design.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead large technical deliverables from initial problem definition through delivery, often across multiple months or quarters.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design and develop backend systems for vulnerability and dependency management, including security report ingestion, storage, indexing, querying, and integrations with key third-party systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and improve systems using Ruby on Rails and PostgreSQL, and contribute to newer services using technologies such as Go or Rust where appropriate.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Shape technical plans, break down complex work, and help other engineers deliver effectively.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work directly with product, design, frontend, and engineering partners to make clear decisions, resolve constraints, and deliver measurable progress.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Influence the team&#39;s product and technical roadmap through hands-on investigation, clear proposals, and iterative delivery that demonstrates progress in each monthly release cycle.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Apply a security mindset when designing systems, including considering how GitLab identifies and handles malicious or vulnerable software packages.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define patterns for modular services, provide technical leadership when vulnerability management work spans multiple GitLab areas, and share that expertise across GitLab Security.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span data-sheets-root=&quot;1&quot;&gt;Take part in on-call or operational support where your team’s ownership model requires it.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll bring&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience leading complex backend projects from idea through delivery while remaining hands-on with design and development.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong PostgreSQL experience, including evidence of query optimization, table optimization, and write-ahead log management in data-intensive systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong professional experience with Ruby on Rails or&amp;nbsp; Go and comfort working in Ruby on Rails day to day. Experience with large monoliths is helpful, along with an interest in working across languages and services.&lt;/li&gt;
