&lt;p&gt;*&lt;em&gt;Fortune 500® is a registered trademark of Fortune Media IP Limited, used under license. Claim based on GitLab data. Fortune 100 refers to the top 20% ranked companies in the 2025 Fortune 500 list, published in June 2025. Fortune and Fortune Media IP Limited are not affiliated with, and do not endorse products or services of GitLab.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h2&gt;An overview of this role&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Staff Software Engineer on GitLab&#39;s Authentication team, you&#39;ll be the technical lead for how every user, application, token, and automated agent proves who it is on GitLab.com, Self-Managed, and Dedicated.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re an OAuth 2.0 and OpenID Connect (OIDC) provider for millions of users. We also accept identity from enterprise identity providers through Security Assertion Markup Language (SAML) and Lightweight Directory Access Protocol (LDAP). Behind that sit more than ten token types and several session methods that grew inside the Ruby on Rails monolith. You&#39;ll help us move this work onto GATE, GitLab&#39;s new authentication and authorization platform. GATE exchanges external credentials for short-lived tokens at the edge through a Secure Token Service written in Go.You&#39;ll set our technical direction, lead the hardest protocol and migration work yourself, and help senior engineers own the rest.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our projects include:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li value=&quot;1&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;strong class=&quot;textBold&quot;&gt;OAuth across Cells:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/strong&gt; Making OAuth clients, grants, and tokens work when users and organizations live in different cells&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li value=&quot;2&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;strong class=&quot;textBold&quot;&gt;Global identities:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/strong&gt; One user identity that works across organizations and cells&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li value=&quot;3&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;strong class=&quot;textBold&quot;&gt;Token consolidation:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/strong&gt; Reducing the number of token types and moving token issuance and validation out of the monolith&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li value=&quot;4&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;strong class=&quot;textBold&quot;&gt;Identity for artificial intelligence (AI) agents and workloads:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/strong&gt; OAuth for Model Context Protocol (MCP) clients, workload identity federation, and service identities with narrow scopes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What you&#39;ll do&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li value=&quot;1&quot;&gt;Own the technical direction for authentication protocols at GitLab, including OAuth 2.0, OIDC, SAML, and token exchange, across the Rails monolith and GATE services.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li value=&quot;2&quot;&gt;Write and drive design documents and architecture decision records (ADRs) for multi-quarter work, then break that work into increments that ship behind feature flags.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li value=&quot;3&quot;&gt;Lead migrations that must not break existing customers: token formats, client and grant state, and session behavior on GitLab.com, Self-Managed, and Dedicated.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li value=&quot;4&quot;&gt;Be hands-on in the most complex parts of the code, in Ruby on Rails and Go, and review the designs and merge requests of other engineers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li value=&quot;5&quot;&gt;Agree interface contracts with the GATE Core, GATE Infra, Authorization, and Tenant Scale (Cells and Organizations) teams, and keep them current as the architecture changes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li value=&quot;6&quot;&gt;Treat authentication as a security and availability boundary: threat-model new flows, add rate limits and abuse controls, and lead the technical response to authentication incidents.&lt;/li&gt;
